df1cd6bce62b34f14266f99f662dd0","event_uuid":"3853f49e-886b-44b8-8cbe-036c2a447d22","position":{"commit_sha":"aa62099672f93747c166fd2beb342a7ec1ed455e","position":"1787338954521568001-3853f49e-886b-44b8-8cbe-036c2a447d22"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9c84c6b12576551b66fd30e7160194bf09696d07371328cedb285fddd49f27a3","event_uuid":"2c660e10-c34b-4444-95a4-1a643eae8e30","position":{"commit_sha":"1bc85bec6cc5f3e1a646eb4fbb8a96f25cbe388c","position":"1787339524935329001-2c660e10-c34b-4444-95a4-1a643eae8e30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"79fb5264db515a902ea6ebc0f7480328db1a497e40ac1574e5d4ca0086a74099","event_uuid":"d9e34677-68bd-4b6d-9cd1-eb56fa5600ba","position":{"commit_sha":"6f0e90724bef8ce20f1ec37e3fe7e4be530917af","position":"1787339527974804001-d9e34677-68bd-4b6d-9cd1-eb56fa5600ba"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA/design escalation (2026-08-17), before reproduction or code edits. The missing project-region premise is confirmed, but the proposed value is contradicted by current repository authorities: .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml records successful invocation in account 896586841071 / us-east-1; external-integration.yml defaults both AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION to us-east-1; infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md directs the bot service to us-east-1; compose defaults likewise use us-east-1. The ticket proposal instead names us-west-2 solely from the local frontier-bedrock profile. Pinning that silently would change the project-wide Bedrock endpoint away from the measured CI/service default.\n\nA second contract issue is proven statically: LLMConfig.from_env resolves CLI/env/file into one bedrock_region_name string, discarding origin. resolve_bedrock_region currently labels every configured non-empty value as REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, so a rebar.toml pin cannot truthfully satisfy the ticket AC requiring provider provenance region_source=repo-config without adding source metadata/plumbing.\n\nDecision required. Recommended: pin us-east-1 in rebar.toml, matching measured CI/service authority, and include truthful config-source provenance plumbing in this bug; retain REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION override precedence. Alternatives: pin us-west-2 as the new project default based on the local profile, or leave project config unpinned and classify fresh-shell setup as an operator-profile/env issue. No production edit or gate reproduction has started pending the decision.","timestamp":1787027314462699001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR RULING (recorded verbatim on the operator's behalf, resolving the 2026-08-17 RCA/design escalation): \"Use the same region as the project's other resources [= us-east-1: .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml records measured invocation in account 896586841071/us-east-1; external-integration.yml defaults AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION to us-east-1; infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md and compose defaults likewise]. Provenance labeling may interact with config wiring and env-var handling; to avoid regression and maintain portability across diverse environments, splitting provenance labeling (region_source=repo-config) into a follow-up task is approved.\"\n\nConsequences for this ticket: (1) rebar.toml [llm] pins bedrock_region_name = \"us-east-1\" (NOT us-west-2 as the original Approach text proposed); (2) the provenance AC (region_source=repo-config) is amended to point at an approved follow-up task rather than this change; (3) env-var precedence (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION over the table value) is preserved and pinned by test.","timestamp":1787334943031090001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix landed. Gerrit change 2011 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2011), LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) + Verified +1 (rebar CI bot, run 32512417349, full matrix green), submitted and MERGED as 4fbeb05607 on main (server-side rebase over 2563919111).\n\nWhat landed: rebar.toml [llm] pins bedrock_region_name = \"us-east-1\" (per the operator ruling above — the project's measured region) beside the region-scoped us.* model pins; docs/config.md documents the key and the pin-the-region-beside-region-scoped-model-pins guidance; tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py pins (a) an AWS_PROFILE-only shell (no REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION / AWS_DEFAULT_REGION / AWS_REGION) resolving the region from the discovered rebar.toml table and it reaching the boto3 session explicitly, (b) REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION keeping precedence over the table value, and (c) a repo guard that this checkout pins the region beside its region-scoped model pins (seen RED before the config edit, GREEN after).\n\nOriginal report replicated as resolved: in the fix worktree, env -u REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION -u AWS_DEFAULT_REGION -u AWS_REGION AWS_PROFILE=frontier → LLMConfig.from_env().bedrock_region_name == 'us-east-1'.\n\nAC status: AC1 met (us-east-1 per ruling); AC2 met (profile-only shell resolves; pinned by test at the config seam); AC3 met (existing precedence preserved, now pinned by test); AC4 amended per ruling → follow-up task astatine-pixilated-shrimp (cda8-0f27-b324-4446), linked discovered_from. Closing.","timestamp":1787338888044439001}],"created_at":1786830307260419001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a5dfa318-3d68-434e-b357-24806810b3dd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4dd2-4217-318a-4613"},{"link_uuid":"cdb38a1e-5f86-4278-9681-ffb3475473b6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8274-6714-32b6-48be"},{"link_uuid":"72ce0e61-e00c-4e56-9586-20fc6e6d4011","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"},{"link_uuid":"c9465f2b-93b0-442a-afa4-3e60b8f07d28","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6a9f-a2eb-857d-4589"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nObserved 2026-08-15 while cutting the 0.12.0 release (ticket grassgreen-unfearful-quoll): `rebar review-plan` failed with `LLMConfigError: a bedrock model/provider is configured but no AWS region could be resolved`, returning an unsigned INDETERMINATE and no LLM pass. The overlap step failed the same way (WARNING rebar.llm.overlap.wire: store-wide overlap step failed).\n\nReproduction environment (this checkout, a fresh non-login agent shell):\n- Env: only `AWS_PROFILE=frontier` exported — no `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION`, no `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`, no `AWS_REGION`.\n- `~/.aws/config`: `[profile frontier]` has NO `region` key (login_session only); `[default]` has `region = us-east-1` but is shadowed by AWS_PROFILE=frontier; `[profile frontier-bedrock]` carries `region = us-west-2` + a credential_process chaining to frontier, but is not the active profile.\n- Result: every resolution rung in the documented order (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION > AWS_DEFAULT_REGION > AWS_REGION > boto3 profile resolution) comes up empty and the provider raises.\n\nPrior art: closed bug saintly-letterhigh-yaffle (8274-6714-32b6-48be) added AWS_REGION to the env-var resolution order (the error message now lists it). That fix works but did not close THIS gap: env-var resolution cannot help a shell that exports none of the vars, and the active profile carries no region.\n\nRoot cause (residual): the repo config half is missing. `rebar.toml`'s `[llm]` table pins the Bedrock model IDs (region-scoped `us.` inference profiles, single-sourced from .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml) but does NOT set `bedrock_region_name`, even though the knob exists (src/rebar/llm/config.py:476,599-600 — `_llm_str(table, cli, \"REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION\", \"bedrock_region_name\", None)`). The checkout therefore knows exactly which region its pinned `us.*` profiles live in, yet makes every operator/agent shell rediscover it via ambient env — fresh agent shells (Copilot/Codex tool shells do not inherit login-shell exports) fail closed on every gated operation.\n\n## Approach\nSet `bedrock_region_name` in rebar.toml's `[llm]` table to the region the pinned `us.*` inference profiles are served from (us-east-1 per the 2026-08-21 operator ruling — the project's measured region, superseding this paragraph's original us-west-2 proposal), so the checkout is self-sufficient: any shell with working AWS credentials runs the gates without per-command region injection. Env vars keep precedence (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION overrides the table value) so nothing regresses for operators who pin a different region. Consider recording in docs/config.md that a repo that pins region-scoped Bedrock inference profiles should pin the region beside them.\n\n## File impact\n- rebar.toml — set bedrock_region_name in [llm]\n- docs/config.md — note pairing region-scoped model pins with a pinned region (if guidance is missing)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] rebar.toml's [llm] table sets bedrock_region_name to the region matching the pinned us.* inference profiles.\n- [x] In a shell exporting only AWS_PROFILE=frontier (no REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, or AWS_REGION), `rebar review-plan <id> --status` and an LLM-bearing gate run resolve a region and do not raise LLMConfigError.\n- [x] REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION env var still overrides the rebar.toml value (covered by an existing or new unit test).\n- [x] ~~The verdict's provider provenance records the region and its source as repo-config.~~ Moved by operator ruling (2026-08-21, comment below) to follow-up task astatine-pixilated-shrimp (cda8-0f27-b324-4446, linked discovered_from): truthful region_source labeling needs source-metadata plumbing (LLMConfig.from_env collapses CLI/env/file into one string; resolve_bedrock_region labels every configured value as REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION) and is out of scope for this change.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"pin bedrock_region_name = us-east-1 beside the region-scoped us.* model pins"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document the bedrock_region_name key and the pin-the-region-beside-region-scoped-models guidance"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","reason":"pin the table rung (AWS_PROFILE-only shell resolves from rebar.toml), env precedence over the table, and the repo-toml guard"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6a9f-a2eb-857d-4589"],["relates_to","8274-6714-32b6-48be"],["relates_to","9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2c660e10-c34b-4444-95a4-1a643eae8e30","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["awaiting-user-escalation"],"ticket_id":"adb6-4762-90f6-4e30","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gated LLM ops fail closed in fresh shells: rebar.toml pins region-scoped Bedrock models but not bedrock_region_name","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a690776-d185-45cb-aef0-d81d2a990152","1dff343f-8b0a-40e6-a679-c7cbf74f01f4","164ce339-6ce8-426e-9d04-8b7256b2a0ea","72ce0e61-e00c-4e56-9586-20fc6e6d4011","fac36080-976a-4d65-8bfd-c0e68ab4c4ab","f82bcbb4-82e2-4caf-837d-43a137b00dee","7d6eed02-a3dd-4de9-9b9c-fd768c4ef14e","362a0c5e-6f07-43d6-ba5f-920bc90cb444","c9465f2b-93b0-442a-afa4-3e60b8f07d28","02b4f0cb-4dcd-42e6-bf1e-0e76c429d9ea","3853f49e-886b-44b8-8cbe-036c2a447d22","2c660e10-c34b-4444-95a4-1a643eae8e30","d9e34677-68bd-4b6d-9cd1-eb56fa5600ba"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787341656071248001,"uuid":"897d43c7-db1e-45b3-a9bf-be3b06414f8e"}